SOAPBOX: This is another WQ6X K-o-S Cw contest from WA6TQT's QTH in Anza. 
SOAPBOX: This was another ad-HOC WQ6X remote operation from WA6TQT's QTH in Anza.
SOAPBOX: It was TOUGH to roll out of bed before 6AM.  Also on Saturday was a
SOAPBOX: Toastmasters District Conference and the Evaluation contest; NoT to
SOAPBOX: mention and ARCA Club board meeting to plan next weekend's membership
SOAPBOX: meeting.  As club President I get to mention our club: http://ARCAHAM.Com.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: The King of Spain GiG left me with mixed feelings.  There were periods of
SOAPBOX: HEAVY activity and then, SILENCE.  What made the difference was a 20-meter
SOAPBOX: opening to Europe around 05:00z, despite a solar storm going on the low-bands.
SOAPBOX: We TRULY are in a period of increasing SFI.  
SOAPBOX: 20-meters was like the "olden days".
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: Because signals were weak along with a LoT of QSB EU stations need to
SOAPBOX: SLOW DOWN; especially when your callsign contains a plethora of DITS.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: LooK for a write up on this GiG at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
